{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-threading-link-alexander","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Example","doco:Section"],"label":"ex:threading-link-alexander","kind":"example","title":"Alexander and reduced Alexander polynomial of the threading link $T(2,N)$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-threading-link"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-threading-link","tags":["threading","torus-link","alexander-polynomial","molecular"],"text":"threading-link-alexander.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"ex:threading-link-alexander\"></a><p><strong>Alexander polynomial.</strong>\nFor even <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">N = 2m</code> the torus link <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T(2,2m)</code> has two components and Conway-normalised Alexander polynomial</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\Delta_{T(2,2m)}(t)\n  = \n  \\bigl(t^{1/2} - t^{-1/2}\\bigr) \\, \\frac{t^m - t^{-m}}{t - t^{-1}}.</code></pre>\n<p>Like every link with two or more components, it vanishes at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">t = 1</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Reduced Alexander polynomial.</strong>\nDividing out the factor <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">t^{1/2} - t^{-1/2}</code> gives the reduced polynomial</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\tilde\\Delta_{T(2,2m)}(t)\n  = \n  \\frac{t^m - t^{-m}}{t - t^{-1}}\n  = \n  [m]_t .</code></pre>\n<p>For a two-component link, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tilde\\Delta(1)</code> is the linking number of the two components. Here <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tilde\\Delta_{T(2,2m)}(1) = m = N/2</code>.</p>\n<p>Evaluated at the substrate parameter <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">t = q</code>:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Threading</th>\n<th align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">m</code></th>\n<th><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tilde\\Delta(q)</code></th>\n<th align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tilde\\Delta(1) = \\mathrm{lk}</code></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T(2,2)</code> (Hopf)</td>\n<td align=\"center\">1</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\">1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T(2,4)</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\">2</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q + q^{-1}</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\">2</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T(2,6)</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\">3</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q^2 + 1 + q^{-2}</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\">3</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T(2,8)</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\">4</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q^3 + q + q^{-1} + q^{-3}</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\">4</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/organic-chemistry/threading-link-alexander.md","heading":"Example","number":"19.2.4","page":"b/ex-threading-link-alexander","qa":{"counts":{"pass":40,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":17,"unknown":0,"stale":57}}}
